# Forms

## Inertia useForm — for server-submitted forms

Use `@inertiajs/react` `useForm` for forms that POST/PATCH/DELETE to Rails controllers.

```tsx
import { useForm } from '@inertiajs/react';

const { data, setData, patch, processing, errors } = useForm({
  profile: { name: profile.name, language: profile.preferredAgentLanguage },
});

const handleSubmit = (e: React.FormEvent) => {
  e.preventDefault();
  patch('/profile', { preserveScroll: true });
};
```

**CRITICAL:** `setData` queues a React state update. Never call `patch`/`post` synchronously after `setData` — the old data will be sent. Use `router.patch` with explicit data instead for immediate saves.

## Mantine useForm — for client-only validation

Use `@mantine/form` `useForm` when you need complex client-side validation without server submission (e.g., multi-step wizards, config builders).

## Mantine Components

Use Mantine form controls: `TextInput`, `Select`, `MultiSelect`, `Textarea`, `Switch`, `Checkbox`, `SegmentedControl`. Never use MUI or react-hook-form.
